Description: pwm: imx1: program the period and divider, and fix the duty cycle
 The driver only rewrote PWMS, relied on the boot loader for the period
 and divider, and wrote PWMP - PWMP * duty / period, while the output
 is high for PWMS cycles of each period: duty 0 gave a full-on output.
 pwm-backlight now keeps a PWM with no enable GPIO running at duty 0
 for brightness 0, which turned such a backlight fully on.
 .
 Program the period from PERCLK1 with the smallest CLKSEL and prescaler
 that fit, and PWMS as the duty cycle in cycles. Also enable the clocks
 before writing the registers, which only take writes while they run;
 the first configuration after a disable used to be lost.
 .
 Document the i.MX21 PWM, which is the i.MX1's.
